     1	"""Pod safety primitives for the follow-up launchers (internal reviews r8-r9 of reset_pod.sh). Every function fails
     2	closed: a failed listing counts as "pods may still exist", and success needs a successful listing that shows no pod.
     3	Time limits are measured in elapsed seconds, never in loop counts.
     4	
     5	CLI (exit 0 = success):
     6	  podctl.py reconcile NAME [KEEP_ID]          delete every pod named NAME except KEEP_ID; verified by a fresh listing
     7	  podctl.py delete ID SECONDS                 delete one pod and verify it is gone within SECONDS
     8	  podctl.py watchdog NAME HARD_TS DONE_FILE   after DONE_FILE, or from HARD_TS (also writes NAME.blocked): delete every
     9	                                              pod named NAME; exits only with DONE_FILE and SETTLE s of empty listings
    10	  podctl.py record-price NAME ID              print ID's price and raise NAME.acct to it; unknown -> NAME.unpriced, exit 1
    11	  podctl.py may-create NAME HARD_TS           exit 0 only before HARD_TS and while NAME.blocked does not exist
    12	  podctl.py remaining UNTIL_TS                print the seconds left (0 when past)
